01:21:43.000 --> 01:21:53.000
And also, Sura 3, verse 171 through 173 states,

01:21:53.000 --> 01:21:59.000
[3:171] They have good news of GOD 's blessings and grace, and that GOD never fails to reward the believers.

01:21:59.000 --> 01:22:05.000
[3:172] For those who respond to GOD and the messenger, despite all kinds of hardship, and lead a righteous life, a great reward.

01:22:05.000 --> 01:22:15.000
[3:173] When the people say to them, "People have mobilized against you; you shall. fear them," this only strengthens their faith and they say, " GOD suffices us; He is the best Protector."

01:22:16.000 --> 01:22:22.000
It seems to be something that distinguishes the righteous believers from the disbelievers

01:22:22.000 --> 01:22:30.000
and hypocrites, that the righteous are more than willing to, to defend their belief in God,

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:35.000
that they don't turn back, that they stand strong, because they have nothing to fear.

01:22:36.000 --> 01:22:41.000
The only thing they fear is God, and they are defending their belief of God, they have nothing to fear.

01:22:42.000 --> 01:22:44.000
Is there any comment or question?

01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:52.000
Now, go on to the disbelievers.

01:22:52.000 --> 01:22:58.000
[2:6] As for those who disbelieve, it is the same for them; whether you warn them, or not warn them, they cannot believe.*

01:22:58.000 --> 01:23:05.000
[2:7] GOD has sealed their hearts and their hearing, and their eyes are veiled. They have incurred severe retribution.

01:23:08.000 --> 01:23:15.000
In Sura 68, the disbelievers are referred to as compromisers, lowly swears,

01:23:15.000 --> 01:23:21.000
slanders, backbiters, forbidders of charity, transgressors, sinners, unappreciative, and greedy.

01:23:27.000 --> 01:23:28.000
Kathryn: Questions, comments?

